[Black "Introduction: Punish Bad Coordination!"]
[Result "*"]

{ @@HeaderStart@@Punish Bad Coordination!@@HeaderEnd@@  In this chapter, the move or idea which you must find is linked to a lack of coordination in your opponent’s pieces.  Keep in mind these issues which you may be able to use to your advantage: trapped pieces, a lack of free squares, undefended or badly positioned pieces, delayed development, a fragile setup.  The difficulty of these exercises ranges from quite easy to moderately difficult, unless an asterisk indicates that the exercise is more difficult. }
