{ @@HeaderStart@@Evaluate the opportunity!@@HeaderEnd@@  For each exercise in this chapter, I will suggest a possible move. You must say whether the move is good or bad and evaluate the resulting position in the same way as a chess engine: White is winning, Black is winning, White is better, Black is better, or the position is equal or unclear.  You must find the key continuation and explain why the suggested move does or does not work.  This is intended to replicate a game situation, when you must analyse a critical candidate move. The difficulty of these exercises ranges from medium to difficult, unless an asterisk indicates that the exercise is very difficult. }
