[Black "Introduction: Make the Right Choice!"]
[Result "*"]

{ @@HeaderStart@@Make the right choice!@@HeaderEnd@@  In each exercise in this chapter, I will suggest two possible moves. One of them is a blunder! You must decide which is right and, most importantly, the reason why the other one is a mistake.  Generally, if the two moves suggested are quite similar, you must find the key continuation in both lines, in order to discover a final important nuance. If the two moves are very different, you must find a clear refutation of one of them.  This chapter is intended to help you to work on your calculation skills, while developing your sense of danger when you need to rule out a move which seemed good at first glance.  The difficulty of these exercises ranges from medium to difficult, the most challenging ones being marked with an asterisk. }
